ction and processing facilities. It also designs and assembles compressor units for rental; and designs, engineers, and sells compressor components. In addition, the company provides aftermarket services for its compressors; and services related to the installation and start-up of new compressor units. Natural Gas Services Group, Inc. was incorporated in 1998 and is headquartered in Southlake, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Justin C. Jacobs | CEO & Director | Age 50 | Compensation: $1.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 259 people. Revenue per employee of $665K ranks in the bottom quartile among Energy peers, with revenue growing 7%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $8K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Natural Gas Services Group, Inc is a small-cap energy business with a $383M market cap on $172M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +27% over the past three years and +6% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $59M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 2.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.7%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 3.2% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 2.0\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $3.7M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-3689891.0},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Energy peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are ultimately hostage to a price the company does not set, and the long-run energy-transition arc adds a structural overhang.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"ESG-driven capital flight and stranded asset risk \u2014 tightening climate policy and investor mandates raise the cost of capital and risk leaving reserves permanently in the ground.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Growing faster than most Energy peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Energy sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter","Energy ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Natural Gas Services Group Inc (NGS) (Q3 2026) Earnings Call Highlights: Record Rental Revenue ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/natural-gas-services-group-inc-230302742.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794524582.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.818,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Understanding Momentum Shifts in (NGS)","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","li