nue.","Capex runs 3.3x depreciation (70.5% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth.","Its Rule of 40 score is -15, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 3.2%, and institutions hold 94%.","Insider trading is two-way: 2 purchases and 2 sales over the past year, net $3.7M sold.","Shareholder yield is a modest 0.7% (2.2% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 1.1% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake."],"people":["With about 259 employees, each generates about $665K of revenue, 0.3x the Energy median, and revenue has grown 7.2% a year across its filed history.","Free cash flow is negative, at -$226K per employee.","CEO pay is $1.3M (2x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (3/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $8K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"INSUFFICIENT DATA","conv":null,"head":"Not enough data to value it: missing price or fair value.","pros":[],"cons":[],"flags":[],"need":[],"buy_below":null,"vc":null,"med":{"pe":13.5876,"ev_ebitda":7.146,"pfcf":14.6331,"pb":1.7432,"roic":0.0952,"gross_margin":0.2462,"fcf_margin":0.0762,"div_yield":0.0357}},"ticker":"NGS","date":"2026-11-13"}